    "objective": "Fix the silent data-loss defect in ticket promotion (GitHub #22). promote_ticket_outputs calls replace_tree(active_dir/'desired', specs_dir/'current'), and replace_tree does shutil.rmtree(dst) before copying. Because the ticket's desired/ tree is seeded from a different source than specs/current, any file unique to specs/current is destroyed with no warning and no failure. Observed twice: MF-012 and MF-020 both lost specs/current/tests/test_current_ticket_workflow.py, which carried MF-012's budgets retention test; the file was not in the history seal either, so the on-disk copy was the only one. Deleted tests cannot fail, so the loss is invisible exactly when it matters. Promotion must either preserve current-only files or abort loudly enumerating every file it would remove. Silent deletion is not an acceptable default for test files.",
    "outcome": [
      "Chose provenance-aware promotion (seed manifest recorded at open) over repairing the seed filter; the seed repair fixes only the one excluded path and cannot reach paths added to specs/current after the ticket opened (MF-020's refinement-probe/). See design-decision.md.",
      "Retention gate MET: 919 distinct states, depth 21, 11 variables - identical to the MF-020 baseline. No new close-failure path was modelled because the fix preserves and enumerates rather than aborting.",
      "Regression gate MET: the regression suite FAILS 4/6 against the pre-fix replace_tree behaviour (prefix-failure.txt) and passes 6/6 after (postfix-pass.txt).",
      "Repository unit tests 117 -> 123 passing; no regression.",
